# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. `install-agent.sh` is copied into the web bundle and served, so
# whatever line endings the working copy has are the line endings that reach the Raspberry Pi. A
# script checked out with CRLF fails there with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M`, which
# names the interpreter rather than the cause and is a genuinely hard hour to spend.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the development machine, so without this the next checkout would
# convert the file and the build after it would publish the broken version.
*.sh text eol=lf
